\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 7-8 BTC, ETH, SOL, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , TRX, XRP\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,161 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 July 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A Market In Panic}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano (\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 ) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tron (TRX) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ripple (XRP) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) continued to drop over the weekend despite a sharp bounce on Saturday, which saw the cryptocurrency climb back above $58,000. However, selling pressure pushed the price back down, with BTC trading around the $55,600 mark.\par \par \uc2 The sudden drop in the price of BTC can be attributed to a couple of major factors that have led to panic selling, although Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s rebound indicates strong demand at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 A Market In Panic\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) has dropped to levels not seen since February, as the crypto market slumped across the board. This indicates panic selling among investors, although some, like Blocktream founder Adam Beck, have urged investors not to panic and to buy the dip, stating that the market drop is part of a typical bull market pattern. He said in a post on X,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReminder, zoom out. Prior bull runs had half a dozen -30% draw downs too. We\u8217\'20\'19re at about -26% (-27% earlier). In fact, if anything, recent draw-downs seem to be less deep, but people forget the normal bull market pattern. Don\u8217\'20\'19t panic, buy the dip. or buy a bit of $CMSTR with BTC.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The prevailing market panic could have been triggered by the liquidation of the \uc2 German government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin holdings. This, coupled with the expectations that a large number of \uc2 Mt. Gox\uc2  creditors will be looking to monetize their repayments, has spooked the market. Financial analysts believe that many of \uc2 Mt. Gox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former creditors will likely sell their BTC holdings. Data from Coinglass shows that almost $116 million worth of BTC has been liquidated over the past 24 hours. If the selling continues, we could see BTC slip even lower than current levels.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/07/crypto-price-analysis-7-5-btc-eth-sol-dot-ton-shib-ltc-atom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  price has continued its slump, hitting a low not seen since February 2024, as sellers drive the price of the asset down. BTC registered a sharp drop on Thursday, falling by over 5% and dropping below the $60,000 mark to settle at $57,097. This drop also saw BTC lose the 200-day SMA, a crucial level during bull runs. Friday saw intense \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressure that drove BTC to a low of $53,591. However, BTC recovered from this level, indicating strong demand at lower levels, and rose to $56,742, a drop of 0.62%. The weekend began with an increase of almost 3% as buyers entered the market, pushing BTC above the $58,000 mark to $58,309.\par \par \uc2 However, with the 200-day SMA acting as resistance, BTC was unable to move past it and dropped by 4.12% on Sunday. The previous week ended on a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  note and settled at $55,909. The current session saw BTC drop to a low of $54,337 before recovering and moving to its current level of $55,673. The rebound, similar to that of Friday, indicates strong demand at lower levels, which means investors are buying the dip.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/i8iPzavH/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 So, what\u8217\'20\'19s in store for BTC? There are some signs that indicate that it\u8217\'20\'19s not all doom and gloom on the horizon. Thanks to demand, sellers are finding it difficult at lower levels, and bulls are trying their best to reclaim $56,000. With BTC recovering from $54,000 twice, it could act as a level of support, allowing buyers to enter the market. If buyers can control the session, we could see them retest the resistance at the 200-day SMA. If it can close above this level, we could also see a push toward $60,000. The \uc2 RSI\uc2  is also close to the oversold zone, indicating that we could see a relief rally.\par \par \uc2 Should sellers continue to exert control and breach the $54,000 level, a slide toward $50,000 is not out of the realm of possibility.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) has been trading between $2,800 and $4,100 since March, as can be deduced from the price chart. The asset experienced considerable selling activity towards the end of the previous week, dropping by 3.65% on Wednesday and settling at $3,291. The price continued to drop on Thursday, falling by over 7% to $3,059. Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s drop also saw ETH slip below the 200-day SAM. Friday saw ETH slip below the crucial $3,000 mark, as it slipped to $2,983. This was after ETH faced considerable selling pressure and dropped to a day low of $2,824 before sellers were able to push the price back up.\par \par \uc2 ETH was positive on Saturday, registering an increase of almost 2% to push back above $3,000 and settle at $3,069. However, it was back in the red on Sunday as selling pressure above $3,000 pushed the price back in the red, registering a drop of $2,931. The current session sees ETH down marginally as sellers look to push ETH below $2,800. We can see from the price chart that ETH hit a day low of $2,827 before buyers were able to push the price back up. This indicates strong buying demand at lower levels, mirroring what occurred on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/PCqyGzqT/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The $2,800 level could play a crucial role, acting as a critical level of support. If sellers can breach this level, we could see a significant slide that could leave ETH around the $2,500 level. However, should the price recover, it could push back above $3,000 and test the resistance at $3,100. For a sustained push, ETH must push above the 200-day SMA, In such a scenario, we could see the price move towards $3,300, where the 20-day SMA could act as the next crucial level of resistance. Looking at the \uc2 RSI\uc2 , it is currently in the oversold territory, meaning we could see buying activity pick up, pointing to a recovery in the short term.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  (SOL) has seen considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past week, peppered with significant drops and gains. Wednesday saw a drop of 8.53%, leaving the cryptocurrency just above the 20-day SMA at $140.74. Thursday saw an even bigger drop as SOL fell by over 9%, dipping below the 20 and 200-day SMAs to $127.07. The cryptocurrency faced intense selling pressure on Friday as sellers pushed the price to a day low of $121. However, with support building at lower levels, buyers were able to reverse the trend spectacularly, with SOL rising to $134.40 from this level. Despite this increase, it was unable to push above the 200-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/J26XanXR/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted on Saturday, with SOL rising by over 6%, pushing back above the 20 and 200-day SMAs to $143. However, it was back in the red on Sunday, dropping by 7.99% to $131.66. The current session sees SOL trading at $131, with buyers and sellers vying for control. Several factors could dictate the future price movements of SOL. There is strong support at $120, a level tested in the past. This means the bulls will try and defend this level. Should this level be breached, we could see the price slide towards $100.\par \par \uc2 On the flip side, should buyers push SOL upwards, it could face selling pressure around the $140 level, with the 20 and 200-day SMAs converging.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) has seen considerable developments over the past few days. The asset has been down by over 10% over the past month, with the decline driven by several concerns, chief among them being criticism of the Polkadot treasury\u8217\'20\'19s high expenditure. The treasury report claimed that Polkadot would only have two years of budget left if it kept spending at its current rate, prompting considerable criticism from the community. The head ambassador for Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s treasury, Tommi Enenkel, stated in the report,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the current rate of spending, the Treasury has about two years of runway left, although the volatile nature of crypto-denominated treasuries makes it hard to predict with confidence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DOT\u8217\'20\'19s recent price troubles have also put considerable stress on the community. The cryptocurrency fell below its support level briefly on Friday, as it tumbled below $5 to a day low of $4.94. However, strong buying at this level pushed the price up significantly, as DOT rose by 2.34% to climb back above $5. DOT surged by almost 10% on Saturday, climbing above $6 and the 20-day SMA to $6.25. However, it faced selling pressure at this level and fell back in the red on Sunday, dropping by 5.44% to $5.91. The current session sees DOT marginally up as buyers look to reclaim $6 and push DOT back above the 20-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/46cXQ90a/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A breakout above $6 could propel DOT towards $6.50, where it could face its next level of resistance. However, should buyers retake the session, we could see another tumble towards $5.\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has had a mixed weekend after registering a sharp drop of over 11% on Thursday, as it slipped below the 20-day SMA to $0.36. Selling pressure persisted on Friday as it fell below its support level, hitting a low of $0.317 before recovering to close at $0.350, indicating strong demand at lower levels. \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  registered an increase of 6.29% on Saturday, rising to $0.372, but fell back in the red on Sunday, dropping by almost 7% to $0.347, once again below the support level. The current session sees \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  up by 1.44% as buyers look to push the price toward the 20-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/7dvMSEDH/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Buyers are expected to defend the lower levels ($0.30 and $0.25), so the price could stabilize at these levels. Should \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  recover, its first crucial test lies at the 20-day SMA, which is currently placed at $0.381.\par \par \uc2 Tron (TRX) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Tron (TRX) has been on a tear since the beginning of June, as it surged from $0.111 on May 31 to $0.127 by July 1. The past month has seen TRX register an increase of over 10%. However, its uptick had registered a bit of a slowdown as it approached a key resistance level at $0.130. As a result, TRX spent Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday in the red after facing significant selling pressure. In fact, TRX reached a day low of $0.120 on Friday, as sellers pushed the price below the 20-day SMA. However, buyers were able to push the price back to $0.126.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/Si2bHaFo/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 TRX registered an increase of 2.38% on Saturday, rising to $0.129. However, it was unable to move past $0.130 and slipped back into the red on Sunday, dropping by 4% to $0.124. The current session sees the price up marginally, trading at $0.125. The price chart shows that the bulls are buying the dip, keeping the price above the 20-day SMA. Should they start a rally, we could see the $0.130 resistance tested once again. Should this level be broken, we could see TRX move to a high of $0.135.\par \par \uc2 Ripple (XRP) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Ripple (XRP) tanked towards the end of the previous week after slipping below the 20-day SMA on Wednesday. Thursday saw the price crash by over 7%, as bears dragged XRP below $0.45 to $0.433. XRP registered a drop of 1.73% on Friday, settling at $0.425 after dropping to a low of $0.381. The long tail indicates investors are buying the dip, and the presence of strong demand at lower levels. XRP made a strong recovery on Saturday from this buying pressure, rising by 5.64% to $0.449. However, it was unable to move above $0.50 and fell back in the red on Sunday, dropping by nearly 7% to $0.41.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/XTUpXcOc/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The current session saw XRP drop to a day low of $0.40 before buyers bought the dip once again, pushing the price to its current level of $0.430, an increase of over 2%. Looking at the \uc2 RSI\uc2 , we can see that it had dipped into oversold territory on Friday. If XRP can maintain its upward push, we could see the \b \highlight22\uc2 price rise\b0 \highlight\uc2  towards the 20-day SMA, currently at $0.47. However, if sellers retake control, they could attempt to push XRP below $0.40.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020240709ek7800001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , XRP, TON, DOGE,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,720 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 July 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins are showing early signs of buying at lower levels, signaling a possible relief rally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDcvZTFlZmEwNjctMTY2MC00N2UzLWI4NjUtODMwNjAyOGJhZmNjLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 Index (SPX) rose about 2% last week to hit a new lifetime high, while Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) collapsed 11% during the same period to hit its lowest weekly close in four months. This shows that Bitcoin has been underperforming the equity markets in the near term. However, some solace for the Bitcoin bulls comes from maintaining BTC price above the critical support of $56,552.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s weakness has resulted in a pullback in several altcoins, which several investors view as a buying opportunity. According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  July 8 report, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/digital-asset-investments-441-million-inflows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 digital investment products witnessed inflows of $441 million}}}\uc2  last week.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/69058b76-7bae-4b6c-9dcf-9a92b7f097c8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 The major question in every investor\u8217\'20\'19s mind is whether the correction is over or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/is-bitcoin-price-going-to-crash-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whether Bitcoin will fall further}}}\uc2 . While it is difficult to state with certainty, some analysts believe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/5-bullish-arguments-bitcoin-price-bottomed-53k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bottom may be near}}}\uc2 . Analysts from the \uc2 Bitfinex\uc2  exchange said in their July 8 report that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-local-bottom-bitfinex-mt-gox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin may have formed a local bottom}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Will the Bitcoin bulls prevent a drop to $50,000? Will altcoins start a recovery? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts to better understand the current technicals in play.\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 Index is in a strong uptrend. It has consistently been making a new all-time high, indicating that the bulls are firmly in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/56440501-4fff-4114-9ec7-7e91ac37f053.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=TVC%3ASPX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A minor negative in the near term is that the relative strength index (\uc2 RSI\uc2 ) has risen into the overbought territory, suggesting a minor correction or consolidation could be around the corner. The 20-day exponential moving average (5,461) will likely be a strong support. If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the index may reach 5,750 and then 6,000.\par \par \uc2 Bears must quickly yank the price below the 20-day EMA if they want to prevent the upside. If they do that, it may tempt the short-term bulls to book profits. The increased selling pressure may sink the index to the 50-day simple moving average (5,320).\par \par \uc2 U.S. Dollar Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls tried to maintain the U.S. Dollar Index (DXY) above the 105.74 resistance, but the bears had other plans.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/e81a6055-beff-499d-8335-79627cb65002.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=TVC%3ADXY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Strong selling pulled the price below the 20-day EMA (105) on July 3. That encouraged the bears to maintain their pressure, and the index slipped below the 50-day SMA (105) on July 5. This suggests that the bulls are losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to strengthen their position further by pulling the price to the crucial support at 104. Buyers are expected to guard this level with vigor. If the price bounces off 104, the index may consolidate between 104 and 106 for a while.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin closed below the $56,552 support on July 7, but the bears could not maintain the momentum and sink the price below $53,485.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/3415cbc4-6d9d-4bb7-bd5e-e576972762d2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=BINANCE%3ABTCUSDT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The tail on the July 8 candlestick shows that the bulls are aggressively defending the zone between $56,552 and $53,485. The BTC/USDT pair could rise to the 20-day EMA ($60,625), an important resistance to watch out for.\par \par \uc2 If the price breaks down sharply from the 20-day EMA, it will indicate that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies. That will put the $53,485 support at risk of breaking down. The next support on the downside is at $50,000.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if buyers kick the price above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the pair may swing inside the $53,485 to $73,777 range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has fallen to the solid support of $2,850 for the second time within the past four days, indicating intense selling pressure from the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/c7ab40a4-feaa-4766-842c-5d120ed1c9db.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=BINANCE%3AETHUSDT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the $2,850 support cracks, the selling may increase, and the ETH/USDT pair could start a down-move to $2,200. The bulls are expected to vigorously defend this level.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price bounces off the current level and rises above $3,110, it will signal the start of a relief rally to the 20-day EMA ($3,272). This is an important level for the bears to defend because a break above it will signal that the pair may continue to trade inside the large range between $2,850 and $4,094 for some more time.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to start a new downtrend by pulling BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) below $460, but the bulls are attempting to hold on to the support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/8d1c1566-c6ad-40b4-8577-d1c160b8cd74.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=BINANCE%3ABNBUSDT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Buyers must push and maintain the price above the 20-day EMA ($553) to suggest that the pullback may be over. The BNB/USDT pair could then attempt a rally to the 50-day SMA ($597).\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or the 20-day EMA and breaks below $460, it will signal the start of a deeper correction. The pair may plummet to $400 and subsequently to $360.\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has been forming a descending triangle pattern, which will complete on a break and close below $116.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/95425d27-e637-4ed2-aedb-d106c8b179f0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=BINANCE%3ASOLUSDT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages suggest that the bears have the edge, but the positive divergence on the \uc2 RSI\uc2  suggests that the bulls are attempting a comeback. The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the moving averages. That could open the doors for a rally to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 The bears are likely to have other plans. They will try to yank the price below $116 and complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. If they manage to do that, the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair could tumble to $100 and then to $80.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 XRP\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) recovery fizzled out at $0.45 on July 6, suggesting that demand dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/fc34ab32-075b-4329-a7bc-f9fb1d6b56ef.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=BINANCE%3AXRPUSDT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The price has reached near-solid support at $0.41. If the price turns up from the current level, it will signal that the bulls are fiercely defending the $0.41 support. The bulls will then make one more attempt to clear the overhead hurdle at $0.46.\par \par \uc2 On the downside, if the $0.41 level crumbles, the XRP/USDT pair may retest the July 5 low of $0.38. The bulls need to protect this level because if it breaks down, the next stop is likely to be $0.30.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-56k-us-stocks-fresh-all-time-highs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price seesaws near $56K as US stocks post fresh all-time highs}}}\par \par \uc2 Toncoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Toncoin (TON) has been consolidating in an uptrend. The price is stuck between $6.77 and $8.29 for the past few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/57201d0e-81d4-417f-baa1-02d87cf5bd71.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 TON/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=OKX%3AtonUSDT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The TON/USDT pair started a solid recovery from $6.36 on July 5, which met with strong selling pressure near the 20-day EMA ($7.42). This indicates that the bears are active at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 The bulls are unlikely to give up the $6.77 to $6.36 support zone without putting up a fight. If the price rebounds off this zone and rises above the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again try to push the pair toward the resistance of the range.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) relief rally could not even reach the breakdown level of $0.12, indicating that the bears are selling on every minor rise.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/ec120f32-2dee-47f3-b8eb-c289e9e5d8b5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=BINANCE%3ADOGEUSDT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are expected to defend the zone between $0.10 and $0.08 with vigor because if this zone gives way, the DOGE/USDT pair may plunge to $0.06. The deeper the fall, the longer it will take for the next rally to begin.\par \par \uc2 If the price rises from the current level, the bears will try to halt the recovery at $0.12. If buyers overcome this barrier, the pair may rally to the 50-day SMA ($0.14), signaling a potential trend change in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been falling inside a descending channel pattern for several days, indicating that the bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/55fbd08b-efae-46aa-bc89-0d2efce7327b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, TON, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/chart/?symbol=BINANCE%3AADAUSDT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages indicate an advantage to bears, but the positive divergence on the \uc2 RSI\uc2  suggests that the selling pressure could be reduced. The bulls will again try to push the price toward the channel\u8217\'20\'19s resistance line. A break and close above the channel will suggest the start of a robust recovery.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price turns down and breaks below the channel, it will indicate an increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair may then drop to $0.25.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDcvZTFlZmEwNjctMTY2MC00N2UzLWI4NjUtODMwNjAyOGJhZmNjLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240708ek78000e6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Solana\par \b \uc2 Why is Solana (SOL) price down today?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Nancy Lubale \par \uc2 818 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2  price dropped below a key support level and appears at risk of further downside. Cointelegraph explains why.\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), the native cryptocurrency of the Solana network, has dropped over 15% in the last 48 hours to reach a low of $121 on July 1. \uc2 SOL\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s weekly losses stand around 10% and 23% in the 30-day timeframe.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/8df59a03-7761-463a-bab3-5bb6035f7708.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s performance over the last day has been accompanied by a leap in its trading volume, which has increased by 42% to $6.4 billion, asserting the intensity of the sell-side activity. This decrease in price and high trading activity have seen its total market capitalization drop to $61.45 billion, but according to data from CoinMarketCap, \uc2 SOL\uc2  still maintains its position as the fifth largest cryptocurrency.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s look at the top catalysts driving \uc2 SOL\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s price lower.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment dominates the wider crypto market\par \par \uc2 The drawdown in \uc2 SOL\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s price over the last few days is largely attributed to the negative sentiment in the broader crypto market led by intensified Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) selling by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/german-government-bitcoin-transfer-market-impact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 German government}}}\uc2  and expected repayments by the defunct crypto exchange \uc2 Mt. Gox\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 German government\uc2  has transferred more than 3,000 BTC to multiple exchanges over the last two weeks, adding to Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s sell pressure.\par \par \uc2 On June 5, \uc2 Mt. Gox\uc2  added to the pressure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/mt-gox-repayments-bitcoin-bitcoin-cash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transferring 47,229 BTC}}}\uc2 , worth around $2.6 billion, to a new address in its first major move since May, according to data from blockchain tracker Arkham.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/eb8f7257-7688-4b77-b03e-29a0a90e7f87.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ArkhamIntel/status/1809157408280772958"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arkham}}}\par \par \uc2 Sentiment toward crypto has also hit its lowest point since January 2023. On July 5, the Crypto Fear and Greed Index scored 29 out of 100, showing that the market is experiencing peak \u8220\'20\'1Cfear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/923f2e60-e427-4c69-8a0b-dd0ac3f10a8b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto Fear and Greed Index. Source: Alternative.me\par \par \uc2 This fear has led to a risk-off mode among investors, explaining the ongoing correction in crypto prices, including \uc2 SOL\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Decreasing activity on the Solana network\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/solana-sol-ecosystem-overview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana network}}}\uc2  has grown tremendously over the last year, shaking off the effects of the \uc2 FTX\uc2  collapse. High developer activity characterized by airdrops led to the launch of many projects, including successful memecoins like BONK and Dogwifhat (WIF). The blockchain\u8217\'20\'19s total value locked (TVL) has increased by 8,800% since November 2023.\par \par \uc2 However, \uc2 SOL\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest \b \highlight22\uc2 price drop\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows a decrease in onchain activity, as fewer users engage with the network, contributing to the decreasing momentum.\par \par \uc2 Data from DefiLlama reveals the TVL on the \uc2 Solana\uc2  network has decreased by 17% from $4.98 billion on June 5 to $4.11 billion on July 5, suggesting that users and developers are interacting less with the network.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/64c34809-347d-4087-8f75-90a51cecba50.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total value locked on BNB Chain. Source: DefiLlama\par \par \uc2 Data from DappRaddar showed that in a comparison of blockchains by monthly network activity, \uc2 Solana\uc2  emerged as the clear leader, with 352 million transactions over the past month\u8212\'20\'14dwarfing Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s 6.97 million and BNB Chain\u8217\'20\'19s 18.9 million.\par \par \uc2 However, additional data revealed that \uc2 Solana\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s DApp volume has decreased by 29% over the last 30 days. Currently, \uc2 Solana\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 30-day DApp volume stands at $3.52 billion, which is far below that of the Ethereum blockchain ($201.91 billion) and the Tron network ($26.69 billion). Notably, the NFT volume decreased by 46.5% over the same period.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/007b4b5c-81aa-472f-82f9-d95b348e64ad.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Layer-1 blockchains ranked by monthly activity. Source: DappRadar\par \par \uc2 This data indicates a drop in NFT trading and staking, significantly impacting the volume decrease. Moreover, token trading on the blockchain trended lower over the month, adding to the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-7-5-btc-eth-bnb-sol-xrp-doge-ton-ada-avax-shib"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/5: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2  price is in a technical correction\par \par \uc2 From a technical standpoint, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/solana-sol-price-encounters-resistance-near-190-here-is-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL's price}}}\uc2  decline is part of an extended technical correction that started on March 18, when it turned away from its multi-year high of $209. The \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USD pair has dropped by over 32% since.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-07/a62bd230-2719-4f5e-af00-55ecdbedd843.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 As of July 5, \uc2 SOL\uc2  was testing its multi-month horizontal support line of a descending triangle for a potential rebound toward the descending trendline at around $150\u8212\'20\'14up 11% from the current price levels.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, a break below the horizontal support line risks a decline toward the technical target of the descending triangle at $74. Such a move would represent a 45% decline from the current price.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDUvMTg3ZjE5ZWItZGRkOS00YzZiLWIxYTctZDA1ZDQ0ODg3MThkLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240705ek75000e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
